    "excerpt": "Understanding the spiritual and social benefits of giving charity in Islam.",
    "content": "Sadaqah, derived from the Arabic word \"Sidq\" (truth), signifies truthful faith through charitable giving. It is a voluntary act of worship that purifies wealth and soul.\n\n## Types of Sadaqah\n1. Sadaqah Wajibah (obligatory) - includes Sadaqat al-Fitr\n2. Sadaqah Mustahabb (voluntary) - any good deed\n3. Sadaqah Jariyah (perpetual) - ongoing charity like building a well\n\n## Benefits of Sadaqah\n- Increases blessings in wealth\n- Protects from calamities\n- Purifies the soul\n- Strengthens community bonds\n- Earns continuous rewards\n\nThe Prophet (PBUH) said: \"Charity does not decrease wealth.\"\n\nAt Minhaajulhudaa Charity, we facilitate various forms of Sadaqah, ensuring your contributions reach those who need them most. Visit our campaigns page to find a cause that resonates with you.",
